WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.529
In Avengers: Endgame, the heroes who survived
Thanos' destructive snap each faced their

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:08.520
own inner battles, but no one took things
as noticeably hard as Thor did.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:13.360
The fallout of Avengers: Infinity War grew
even more dire three weeks after the fact,

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.900
when the remaining Avengers tracked down the
big purple dude and discovered that he had

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.920
used the Infinity Stones to destroy the Infinity
Stones, which spurred an exasperated Thor

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.880
to take his battle-ax hammer Stormbreaker
and slice Thanos' head clean off.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.280
"You should have gone for the head."

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.960
Fast forward five years after Thanos' quick
beheading, and not all of Earth's Mightiest

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.520
Heroes were doing well.

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:40.700
Wracked with guilt over just barely failing
to stop Thanos in Infinity War, and feeling

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:44.760
as though he was responsible for the death
of his brother Loki and the countless billions

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.719
who died in the snap, Thor turned to the bottle,
the joystick, and the snack cupboard for comfort.

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:53.899
For most of Avengers: Endgame, Thor looked
less like the chiseled God of Thunder and

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:55.899
more like the Dude from Big Lebowski.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:00.930
His hair was long and matted, his beard thick
and full, his physique larger and without

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:05.440
tone, and his disposition not nearly as chipper
or confident as it once was.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.880
He found pleasure in grabbing a headset and
talking smack to kids playing Fortnite.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.160
He sought happiness in drinking beer — and
lots of it.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.940
He even guarded himself from hurt by banning
Thanos' name from being spoken in his house

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:21.800
in New Asgard, drunkenly rambled during the
Time Heist meeting at Avengers HQ, and continuously

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.660
doubted his own abilities.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.340
So what does Chris Hemsworth have to say about
Thor's evolution from the strongest Avenger

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.020
to the down-in-the-dumps guy we saw in Avengers:
Endgame?

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.940
Like it or not, it was his idea.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.260
The actor opened up to USA Today ahead of
Endgame's theatrical debut, and discussed

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.260
the dramatic change Thor underwent.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.310
He hinted that it was, at least partially,
his idea:

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.800
"I just had an opinion.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.540
I wanted to do something different this time."

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:50.300
“We sat for many hours and days and discussed
kind of how far we could push it and what

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.620
we could do different.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.640
It was great that was welcomed."

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.060
This isn't the first transformation Thor has
experienced during his time in the Marvel

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.560
Cinematic Universe, of course — though it's
probably the most shocking.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:08.320
For the first few movies of the MCU in which
he appeared, Thor had long, yellow-blonde

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.060
hair — and was also self-important, serious,
and kind of a brat.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:17.020
When it came time to close off Thor's three-film
series with Thor: Ragnarok, however, Taika

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.380
Waititi stepped behind the helm and brought
a completely new version of Thor to the silver

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:20.920
screen.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.400
"What happened to your hair?”

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.400
“Some creepy, old man cut it off.”

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.800
“It looks good.”

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.920
“Oh, thanks."

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:31.719
He had a cropped 'do, a radically more selfless
personality, an ability to make tough choices

00:02:31.719 --> 00:02:35.680
for the greater good and a sense of humor
that solidified him as one of the most naturally

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.830
funny characters in the MCU.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:42.220
Since Thor remained largely the same from
Thor: Ragnarok to Avengers: Infinity War,

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:45.420
it seems there could be something of a pattern
here: a certain iteration of Thor may only

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.820
be able to exist in a limited number of Marvel
movies.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.499
Uptight, long-haired Thor was in the hero's
first two trilogy films, along with the first

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.060
two Avengers movies.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:58.760
Goofy, kind-hearted, short-haired Thor was
in Ragnarok and Infinity War.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:03.159
Now, chubby and self-conscious Thor is in
Avengers: Endgame — and will likely appear

00:03:03.159 --> 00:03:07.870
in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, as the
final moments of Endgame saw Thor join the

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.319
galaxy-faring heroes on their new mission.

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:14.790
Unless Hemsworth has another chat with Marvel
bigwigs on how to give Thor another revamping,

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.469
theThor featured in Endgame could be back
again pretty soon.

